; `pick FACT` (without `with`) whose fact ends in an application with brackets, `P(c)`: the
; tokens were parsed twice, and the first parse changed the `)` -- the line then read as an
; unclosed bracket ("unexpected end of file"), with a block after it even a crash ("too many
; dedents"). Found by the consistency check of tutorial lesson 09 (2026-10-09).
load logic, numbers
bool P, Q
arity P 1
const P, Q
use exists $x > 0 P($x)
use forall $x ((($x > 0) and P($x)) implies Q)
pick c > 0 and P(c)
    Q
Q
pick d > 0 and P(d)
    Q
pick e with e > 0 and P(e)
    Q
Q
